* mark.a -- writes the run-boundary line into RESULTS/report.** This exists so the suite needs no external utility whatsoever. The* obvious way to write a boundary line is `echo RUN prebuilt`, but `echo`* lives in the system's own command directory, and runall has already* pointed CHX at the suite's CMDS so that the tests resolve by bare name --* at which point `echo` is unfindable and the run dies on its first line.** The 6809 suite hits the same wall and solves it by telling the operator* to `load procs` and `load runb` before starting, which is two more things* to get wrong and two more reasons a run can fail with a path error that* looks like a broken disk. Owning the one line of output we need removes* the problem instead of documenting it.** The report is append-only, so this line is what lets a later reader split* a report containing several runs back into separate runs.*Prgrm set 1Objct set 1ReEnt set $80Type_Lang set (Prgrm<<8)+ObjctAttr_Rev set (ReEnt<<8)+1IWrite set $8AFExit set $06* psect mark,Type_Lang,Attr_Rev,0,1024,startstart lea msg(pc),a0 moveq #MSGLEN,d1 moveq #1,d0 trap #0 dc.w IWrite moveq #0,d1 trap #0 dc.w FExit*msg dc.b "RUN prebuilt",13MSGLEN equ *-msg ends